<title>SOUTH AFRICA: No question S.Africa Telkom deal signed - spokesman.</title>
<headline>No question S.Africa Telkom deal signed - spokesman.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A privatisation deal between South Africa's state telecommunications utility Telkom and a Malaysian-U.S. consortium was signed on Wednesday, a spokesman for South African President Nelson Mandela said.</p>
<p>Spokesman Parks Mankahlana made the clarification after Mandela, speaking to Indian businessmen in New Delhi on Friday caused some confusion by saying the privatisation was &quot;in the final stages of negotiation&quot;.</p>
<p>It appears that Mandela mis-spoke.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, he was talking about the same thing. The deal was definitely signed on Wednesday,&quot; Mankahlana told Reuters.</p>
<p>The deal is the biggest direct investment in South Africa yet, Telekom Malaysia Bhd partnered by U.S.-based SBC Communications Inc bought a 30 percent stake in Telkom for $1.261 billion (5.58 billion rand).</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
